body:
**Shape.** A reassignment of an owned field through a binding that is moved-from.

```bezel
module Probe;

public sealed class Q
  private _id: int;
  public constructor(id: int)
    _id := id;
  end constructor;
  destructor
    Console.WriteLine($"D:{_id}");
  end destructor;
  public method Use()
    Console.WriteLine($"U:{_id}");
  end Use;
end Q;

public sealed class R
  private _id: int;
  public owned f: Q;
  public constructor(id: int, owned q: Q)
    _id := id;
    f := q;
  end constructor;
  destructor
    Console.WriteLine($"D:{_id}");
  end destructor;
  public method Use()
    Console.WriteLine($"U:{_id}");
  end Use;
  public static method Take(owned r: R)
    using var k := move r;
  end Take;
  public static method Body()
    var b := new R(2, new Q(1));
    R.Take(move b);                   // b is moved-from
    b.f := new Q(3);                  // a field store through a moved-from binding: K1.3 error; accepted, SIGSEGV
  end Body;
end R;

public class Program
  public static method Main(): int
    R.Body();
    Console.WriteLine("END");
    return 0;
  end Main;
end Program;
```

**Measured on r35.** Zero diagnostics in both modes; `--checked-disposal` and `--unchecked-disposal` both print `D:2 D:1` (the callee's disposal) and then **SIGSEGV** (exit 139) at the store — the moved-from slot is null, and no `DisposedAccessException` is possible because the object was never *disposed* under this binding, it was transferred. A plain read (`b.Use()`) at the same point is correctly rejected (`owned value in \`b\` was already moved out`); the field-store LHS is the gap. Sibling: `b.f := q;` with an owned `q` (K3.1 store) behaves the same.

**Spec (v0.345).** K1.3 (§28.3.1): *"moved-from — the obligation has transferred out; the binding is unreadable until reassigned"*; K3.11's reassignment is of the **binding** (`b := …`), not of a field reached through it — `b.f := e` is a read of `b` (K1.5: a field read lends from the holder, so the holder must be readable). Expected: a compile error at `b.f := …` naming the moved-from binding.

**Differential numbers.** 30 of 3,000 sampled programs in the `fields` fragment (vars 3 / len 4, no replacing move): every model `K1.3-read-of-moved` rejection at a slot store (`fst`) through a moved-from holder is accepted by r35 and crashes.

**Measured on r35** (`bezelc 0.0.0-f6863e62`, the 2026-10-27 release build; main may have moved since). Found by the model-vs-compiler differential (`scratch/bzdiff`, proposal 0047 §5.3 / soundness README §3.2): the executable ownership model (bzcore L1, spec v0.345) and `bezelc` disagree on this program; the model's verdict is the spec's sentence quoted above.
